elefoonnummer"=>"jkl", "data"=>[{"datum"=>"adsf"}], "functie"=>"jkl", "aanmelding-title"=>"asdf", "aanmelding-tekst"=>"jkl", "button-submit"=>"jkl", "bedrijf"=>"jkl", "button-reset"=>"jkl", "pagina-afbeelding"=>"asdf", "success-text"=>"jkl", "button-terug"=>"jkl", "welke"=>"jkl", "placeholder-answer"=>"jkl", "title"=>"asdf", "reden"=>"jkl", "aanmelding-zoom"=>"jkl", "email"=>"kjl", "hoe"=>"jkl", "naam"=>"jkl"}}, "en"=>{"global"=>{"nederlands"=>"Dutch", "english"=>"English", "site_title"=>"Human Connection"}, "nav"=>{"home_url"=>"/", "logo_alt_text"=>"Human Connection Logo", "wie_wij_zijn_url"=>"/who-we-are/", "wie_wij_zijn_text"=>"Who we are", "team_base_url"=>"/team/", "wat_wij_doen_text"=>"What we do", "hoe_wij_werken_url"=>"/how-we-work/", "hoe_wij_werken_text"=>"How we work", "ctp-contact"=>"/ctp-contact/", "wat_wij_doen_url"=>"/what-we-do/", "connect_to_perform_url"=>"/connect-to-perform/", "connect_to_perform_text"=>"Connect to Perform", "vertrouwenspersoon_url"=>"/confidential-advisor/", "vertrouwenspersoon_text"=>"Confidential Advisor", "coaching_url"=>"/coaching/", "coaching_text"=>"Coaching", "contact_text"=>"Contact", "contact_url"=>"/contact/", "werken_bij_url"=>"/work-with-us/", "werken_bij_text"=>"Work with us", "lang_nl"=>"Nederlands", "lang_en"=>"English", "call_us"=>"Call us", "email_us"=>"Email us", "succes_url"=>"/success/"}, "home"=>{"slogan"=>"Change is human work", "landing-tekt"=>"Human Connection is an organizational consultancy focused on the human side of organizations. From various roles, we guide leaders, teams, and individual professionals to develop and work (together) more proactively.\n\nWe always work custom-made, with a broad perspective on people in their context, healthy business operations, and the development of organizational culture.\n\nWe are experienced in a wide field, love a complex challenge, and look at possibilities with an optimistic view.", "pagina-afbeelding"=>"/assets/images/upload/parachute.jpg", "waar-wij-voor-staan"=>"What we stand for", "waar-wijvoor-staan-tekst"=>"We do what we say and say what we do. Both in how we collaborate internally within our company, and how we collaborate with our clients. We always work:", "waarde-1-titel"=>"In Connection", "waarde-1-tekst"=>"Synergy arises where people are connected with themselves, with each other, and with the purpose of the organization.\n\nSelf-awareness, ownership, engagement, and taking responsibility are key here. We stand for this ourselves, and it is also exactly what we help our clients with. We bring our own personalities, experiences, and 'humanity' into everything we do.", "waarde-1-afbeelding"=>"/assets/images/upload/icoon3dun.png", "waarde-2-titel"=>"In Trust", "waarde-2-tekst"=>"For us, trust is the foundation from which we work. Among ourselves as colleagues and in collaboration with our clients. It is our second nature, wherever we work, to build trust between people and in organizations as a whole.\n\nWe approach people and their issues positively: as a principle, we cherish great confidence in everyone's good intentions, capabilities, and resilience.", "waarde-2-afbeelding"=>"/assets/images/upload/icoon2dun.png", "waarde-3-titel"=>"In Context", "waarde-3-tekst"=>"We view every question, no matter how large or small, with a broad perspective. 'What is really going on here? What patterns are at play?'\n\nPrecisely the interplay between various factors (such as organizational structure, way of working, culture, the changing external world) determines success. That is why we closely align with the context of an organization and people, and everything we do is custom-made.", "waarde-3-afbeelding"=>"/assets/images/upload/icoon1dun.png", "wat-wij-doen"=>"What we do", "wat-wij-doen-tekst"=>"We approach every issue with an organization-wide perspective. We do this based on several areas of expertise:", "wat-wij-doen-1-titel"=>"Organizational Development & Team Development", "wat-wij-doen-1-tekst"=>"We advise and guide teams and organizations during changes. Through longer trajectories (lasting cultural change or reorganizations), shorter interventions (teambuilding and proactive behavior), and 'everything in between'.\n\nExamples include:\n\n* Transformation towards more self-management \n* Facilitating in-depth conversations and powerful decision-making. \n* Culture development: better performance and a more (pro)active culture. \n* Reorganizations, mergers, optimizing collaborations \n* Compliance and integrity issues \n* Implementing and guiding Agile/Scrum", "wat-wij-doen-1-contact"=>"**Want to know more?**\\\nFor example, contact Sjef or Zilla.", "wat-wij-doen-1-button"=>"Contact Sjef", "wat-wij-doen-1-link"=>"/team/sjef-van-gool/", "wat-wij-doen-2-titel"=>"Interim Management", "wat-wij-doen-2-tekst"=>"As interim professionals, we become part of the organization for a period. As a manager or director, together with the strategic partners present in the organization, we proactively set a course that aligns with the bigger picture. We enjoy doing this in combination with a change assignment.\n\nWe do this, for example, in the areas of:\n\n* Change management \n* HR management \n* Strategy implementation \n* ICT management \n* L&D Professional", "wat-wij-doen-2-contact"=>"**Want to know more?**\\\nFor example, contact Meggie or Dorothé.", "wat-wij-doen-2-button"=>"Contact Meggie", "wat-wij-doen-2-link"=>"/team/meggie-van-de-bunt/", "wat-wij-doen-3-titel"=>"Learning & Development", "wat-wij-doen-3-tekst"=>"We guide personal and professional development for directors, managers, and professionals. Personal leadership and personal effectiveness are important themes here.\n\nWe advise on the most effective approach and design and facilitate workshops or programs such as:\n\n* Development trajectories and training programs \n* Leadership programs \n* Intervision (Peer consultation) \n* [Individual coaching](https://www.humanc.nl/coaching/) \n* Talent management and trainee programs \n* Designing an effective learning infrastructure", "wat-wij-doen-3-contact"=>"**Want to know more?**\\\nFor example, contact Marit or Annet.", "wat-wij-doen-3-button"=>"Contact Marit", "hoe-wij-werken"=>"Want to know more about how we work?", "wat-wij-doen-3-link"=>"/team/marit-weiss/", "wie-wij-zijn"=>"Who we are", "actievraag"=>"What challenges are you facing in your organization?", "actievraag-subtitel"=>"Discover how we can help with this.", "actievraag-button"=>"Get in touch with us", "partners-titel"=>"Worked with, among others:", "contact-titel"=>"Contact", "contact-omschrijving"=>"We would like to get in touch with you. Call or email one of our colleagues directly, or fill in the form below.", "contact-naam"=>"Name", "contact-email"=>"E-mail", "contact-onderwerp"=>"Subject", "contact-bericht"=>"Question/Message", "contact_placeholder"=>"Your answer", "contact_label_naam"=>"Name*", "contact_label_onderwerp"=>"Subject*", "contact_label_email"=>"Email*", "contact_label_bericht"=>"Question/Message*", "contact_submit_button"=>"Send message", "contact_org_name"=>"Human Connection", "uitnodiging"=>"Or visit us at our picturesque Amsterdam office:", "postcode"=>"1013 GA Amsterdam", "contact-button"=>"Send Message", "adres"=>"Singel 2a", "afbeelding-kantoor"=>"/assets/images/upload/kantoor.png"}, "hoe-wij-werken"=>{"title"=>"How we work", "landing-tekst"=>"Everything we do is custom-made, because every change has its own dynamics, complexity, and pace.\n\nWe have extensive knowledge in-house and are seasoned in a number of methodologies. Where necessary, we deploy these. We use theories and models as a collective frame of reference and common language. The emphasis for us is always on direct applicability in daily work.", "pagina-afbeelding"=>"/assets/images/upload/impact.jpg", "waar-wij-voor-staan"=>"Methods and formats", "waar-wijvoor-staan-tekst"=>"Examples of methods and formats are: Connect to Perform culture development, agile/scrum, deep democracy, business drawing, Discovery Insights, Voice Dialogue, irreversible change, designing with the learning infrastructure, various creative formats\n\nBeing development-oriented, we stay up to date with the latest insights in the field of theory and practice.", "waarde-1-titel"=>"1. Contact and context", "waarde-1-tekst"=>"It starts with personal contact. Together with a client, we examine what the context of the organization and the people on the work floor is. We look at the whole with a broad perspective: 'what is really going on here?'", "waarde-1-afbeelding"=>"", "waarde-2-titel"=>"2. Pragmatic design and advice", "waarde-2-tekst"=>"Based on this, we provide advice on an effective approach. In doing so, we let the organization stay in control as much as possible. We design ahead, preferably together with the people involved. We create realistic expectations and frameworks.", "waarde-2-afbeelding"=>"", "waarde-3-titel"=>"3.  Guidance", "waarde-3-tekst"=>"We guide the implementation step by step, so adjustment is always possible. We work methodically where necessary. We understand the dynamics and complexity of organizations and always have an eye for the individual person and their work and private context.", "waarde-3-afbeelding"=>"", "waarde-4-titel"=>"4. Pushing through until it really works​", "waarde-4-tekst"=>"Especially at difficult moments, or when things seem too quiet, we help to push through.  We help turn awareness into action on the work floor. Not rigidly sticking to the 'plan from six months ago', but again in relation to the current course and circumstances of the organization. With a focus on long-term results.​", "waarde-4-afbeelding"=>"", "waarde-5-titel"=>"5. Evaluating", "waarde-5-tekst"=>"Development is never 'finished'. However, we find it important that our clients know how to continue independently for a while after our guidance. We help to evaluate sharply and anticipate future developments. And we always keep the line open for a quick sparring session or catch-up.", "waarde-5-afbeelding"=>""}, "coaching"=>{"title"=>"Coaching", "landing-tekst"=>"Do you want more self-insight, a better handle on your approach to certain matters, to break free from certain patterns, or concrete tools to be more effective in your work?\n\nWith individual coaching, we help you in a tailored way. In a manner (live, outdoors, online, on the job) and rhythm (a quick boost or rather a calmer, somewhat longer trajectory?) that suits you.\n\nBased on an intake, you choose the coach that suits you, and together you determine what the coaching trajectory looks like. We tailor every coaching trajectory to your needs, goals, and context. On one hand, this involves depth: what is the background of your coaching question? And on the other hand, practical application: translating the insights you gain into your life and work.\n\nWe coach from the work floor up to the executive level. Independently and confidentially. It can be linked to an organizational development trajectory or leadership development. But also for individuals looking for more balance or the next career step.", "pagina-afbeelding"=>"/assets/images/upload/kompas.jpg", "pagina-titel"=>"Coaching", "coaching-tekst"=>"**Coaching Themes**\n\nThe goal and theme of the coaching trajectory are always individually determined and often a combination of multiple elements. In practice, we often work with the following themes:\n\n* Personal development \n* Communication \n* Balance and resilience | stress, burnout \n* Career development\n\n\\\n**Methods and Forms** \\\nWe work with methods and materials from various management theories, psychology, and approaches such as Voice Dialogue, Co-active coaching, ACT, Insights, and Deep Democracy. \\\n\\\nIn a coaching trajectory, various conversation forms and elements can be used, such as: conversations (live, online, or walking), in-depth assignments, practical assignments, coaching on the job, three-way conversations with the manager, reading material, background articles, reflection assignments, tests, and videos.\n\n**Always Custom-Made** \\\nWe help you gain insight into your behavioral patterns, explore your comfort zone, and implement sustainable changes. This way, you work not only on your professional growth but also on a healthier balance and more resilience.\n\nSo, we don't do 'standard programs'. It's not a matter of 'give me module 2 and session type x'. Instead, we look together with you at what works. In your context, with your goals, wishes, and own wisdom. \\\n\\\n**The Coaches** \\\nA large number of our colleagues are professional coaches. We all have our own background and style. What we agree on is that we stand for professionalism, confidentiality, and a broad perspective on the person, in their context.\n\nBelow you will find the names of colleagues who coach: [](https://www.humanc.nl/team/anne-boertien/)[Marit](https://www.humanc.nl/team/marit-weiss/), [Anne](https://www.humanc.nl/team/anne-boertien/), [Jojanneke](https://www.humanc.nl/team/jojanneke-van-goinga/), [Meggie,](https://www.humanc.nl/team/meggie-van-de-bunt/) [Alexander, ](https://www.humanc.nl/team/gerke-visser/)[Gerke,](https://www.humanc.nl/team/gerke-visser/) [Petra,](https://www.humanc.nl/team/petra-berry/) [Willemijn](https://www.humanc.nl/team/willemijn-dekker/),[ Zilla](https://www.humanc.nl/team/zilla-uiterwijk/) and [Sjef.](https://www.humanc.nl/team/sjef-van-gool/)\\\n\\\n**Interested?**\\\nContact one of our colleagues directly, or for more information contact [Marit.](https://www.humanc.nl/team/marit-weiss/)"}, "connect-to-perform"=>{"title"=>"Connect to Perform", "pagina-afbeelding"=>"/assets/images/upload/verandering-transitie.jpg", "landing-tekst"=>"‘Connect to Perform’ is the philosophy that forms the basis for Human Connection’s consultancy work. It demonstrates how teams and organizations can move towards a more effective and pleasant way of working by making (mutual) connections. To bridge the gap between ’theory’ and ‘applying it yourself’, we have designed a game that is played with great success in organizations and during our open evenings.", "methoden"=>"Connect to Perform Culture Development", "methoden-tekst"=>" ", "pagina-illustratie"=>"/assets/images/upload/connect-to-perform-ingevuld.jpg", "werkwijze-titel"=>"Connect to Perform: the game ", "werkwijze-tekst"=>"During the game, using a fictional situation, you gain insight into the methodology and possible interventions to develop organizational culture and performance. It becomes clear how you can identify which development phase an organization (or team) culture is in. Based on practical examples, you playfully see what is needed to take the next development step and what things actually backfire.\n\nYou gain insight into about fifty different interventions applicable in work practice, to influence the behavior and culture of a team and organization. In short, in a few hours, you are interactively immersed in our successful approach on how to make more impact with your team.", "werkvorm-titel"=>"Open Game Evening", "werkvorm-tekst"=>"As an introduction, we organize an open game evening several times a year, nowadays often online, where our relations and interested parties are welcome to get acquainted with this methodology. (participation is completely free and without further obligations) Via a login to our online learning portal, you get access to videos with explanations and background information. Moreover, experience shows that it is very interesting to exchange thoughts with people you didn't know before, working in diverse organizations.\n\nIn organizations, we play the game (online or offline) in MT trajectories or leadership programs. We have different formats, depending on the time and interest of the target group, and we also customize the content of the game where necessary. The translation to the work context, in light of the organization's strategy, and also the concretization ‘what will I do with it tomorrow’ are important parts of the debriefing and any follow-up.\n\nThe game can also be requested as a standalone workshop. Think of a half or full day, online or offline, for a group of 4 to 80 participants. For more information, please send an email to Jojanneke van Goïnga.\n", "button1"=>"Learn more about Connect to Perform", "more-info"=>"/assets/images/upload/connect_to_perform.pdf", "button2"=>"Sign up here for the open game evening"}, "werken-bij"=>{"title"=>"Working at", "vacature-open"=>false, "pagina-afbeelding"=>"/assets/images/upload/parachute.jpg", "landing-tekst"=>"We are looking for someone who can stand in front of a group with self-confidence and a fresh perspective, and is also capable of conducting individual coaching sessions. Your fresh perspective and creativity are very welcome, as is your ability to, regardless of the circumstances, deal constructively with group dynamics. Your perspective is broader than personal development alone; you are interested in organizational development, from strategy to execution, and are eager to learn more about it.", "kop"=>"As coach/facilitator of development programs", "wat-je-doet"=>"What You'll Do:", "wat-je-doet-tekst"=>"You create custom programs in which employees and managers of organizations can develop themselves. Think of a year-long trajectory 'Personal Leadership', a 'Masterclass trajectory for talent', or other forms of trainee or leadership programs.\n\nWe are looking for someone who can stand in front of a group with self-confidence and a fresh perspective, and is also capable of conducting individual coaching sessions. Your fresh perspective and creativity are very welcome, as is your ability to, regardless of the circumstances, deal constructively with group dynamics. Your perspective is broader than personal development alone; you are interested in organizational development, from strategy to execution, and are eager to learn more about it. You can collaborate well and are simultaneously autonomous enough to find your own way in our small-scale, flat organization. Mirroring clients, colleagues, and also turning the spotlight on yourself, you find an appealing challenge.", "wat-we-bieden"=>"What We Offer You:", "wat-we-bieden-tekst"=>"* A salary that matches your knowledge and experience. * An end-of-year bonus based on the profit made together. * A laptop, phone, 1st class public transport card, everything you need to work well hybridly, and good secondary benefits. * An office in the heart of Amsterdam, a 2-minute walk from CS (Central Station) (where you only need to be when working on assignments with colleagues).", "contact"=>"Contact Meggie via [meggie@humanc.nl](#) or 06 50 83 56 58.", "uitzendbureaus"=>"Temporary employment or recruitment agencies need not respond to this vacancy."}, "vertrouwenspersoon"=>{"title"=>"Confidential Advisor", "landing-tekst"=>"**Confidential Advisor and prevention as a priority for a socially safe workplace**\n\nIn a time where the emphasis is increasingly placed on **creating a healthy and pleasant work climate**, the question arises: how can organizations **guarantee a safe environment for their employees?** Appointing an (internal) confidential advisor is a frequently chosen **first step** for companies. To actually create and maintain a safe working environment, **broader measures and sometimes even a culture change are also necessary.**\n\nIntegrating **social safety in the workplace** turns out to be a crucial factor in striving for **a sustainably healthy organization.**\n\nIf there is a **pleasant learning and working climate, results are better, work is more effective, and more innovation** is possible. But what exactly does this entail, and how can organizations achieve this?", "pagina-afbeelding"=>"/assets/images/upload/sociale-veiligheid.webp", "pagina-titel"=>"Confidential Advisor", "vertrouwenspersoon-tekst"=>"### What is a socially safe workplace?\n\nEvery workplace is different, every company culture is different. Yet, there are several elements that indicate a socially safe workplace:\n\n* Employees express themselves easily. \n* They *also* talk about bottlenecks in the execution of their work. \n* They talk openly and freely. \n* They speak out without fear of consequences.\n\n### Broad, systemic approach\n\nHuman Connection distinguishes itself through a broader approach to creating a socially safe workplace, where a confidential advisor forms an essential part.\n\nThe focus is on preventive measures, in addition to offering help with context analysis, interventions, and guidance, should escalation occur. We do this with a well-thought-out and systemic approach that we have been using and further developing since 1998. For more information, see [here](https://www.humanc.nl/hoe-wij-werken/).\n\n### Human Connection offers:\n\n* Certified confidential advisors \n* Each confidential advisor brings at least one additional expertise \n* Replacement during illness or vacation * Mutual intervision (peer consultation), unlocks an even broader perspective on issues \n* Experience involving the entire organization at the start, continuation, and execution of (change) projects.\n\n### Want to know more?\n\nDo you want to know more about how Human Connection views the role of the confidential advisor and prevention as a priority within a healthy workplace? Download our whitepaper here with key factors for a socially safe working environment."}, "ctp-contact"=>{"title"=>"Connect to perform", "pagina-afbeelding"=>"/assets/images/upload/verandering-transitie.jpg", "landing-tekst"=>"As an introduction, we organize an open game evening several times a year,  often online these days, where our contacts and interested parties are welcome  to become familiar with this methodology. (Participation is completely free  and without further obligation). Through a login to our online learning portal,  you gain access to videos with explanations and background information.  Furthermore, experience shows it's very interesting to exchange thoughts  with people you haven't met before, working in various organizations.", "aanmelding-title"=>"Game Evening Registration Form", "aanmelding-zoom"=>" ", "aanmelding-tekst"=>"Fill in your details here to register for the game evening.", "naam"=>"Name*", "email"=>"Email*", "bedrijf"=>"Company*", "functie"=>"Position*", "telefoonnummer"=>"Phone Number*", "welke"=>"Which evening are you registering for?*", "data"=>[{"datum"=>"Monday October 6th: 19:30-21:45."}], "hoe"=>"Via whom or how did you hear about the Connect to Perform evening?", "reden"=>"What is your reason for registering?", "success"=>"Thank you for registering!", "success-text"=>"Thanks for registering, we're happy you'll be joining!\n\nFor now, you don't need to do anything except put the date in your calendar.\n\nAbout a week beforehand, you will receive a preparation email with more information.\n\nIf you have any questions before then, please contact jojanneke@humanc.nl", "button-terug"=>"Back to the homepage", "placeholder-answer"=>"Your answer", "button-submit"=>"Send form", "button-reset"=>"Reset form"}}}}:ET